	faithHeading="Faith and the Bible in Hungary"
	faithBodyHtml={`<p>The 2022 census counted <strong>9,603,634 people</strong> on 1 October 2022. The religion question was voluntary and <strong>60%</strong> answered it. Of those who answered, <strong>50%</strong> (2.9 million) were Catholic, <strong>16%</strong> Reformed and <strong>3.1%</strong> Lutheran, while <strong>27%</strong> said they are not religious (Hungarian Central Statistical Office, KSH).</p><p>The Hungarian Bible is old here. The first complete New Testament was printed in 1541, the Calvinist Károli Bible followed at Vizsoly in 1590, and the Catholic Káldi Bible in 1626; the Károli translation&rsquo;s 1908 edition was widely adopted.</p><p>The invitation of Father&rsquo;s Heart Bible&trade; is a personal one: read the same Word in clear Hungarian, and meet in it a Father.</p>`}
